            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45149",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service due to excessive memory allocation when expanding large numeric ranges"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. From 5.0.0 to before 5.0.6, the max option was being applied too late. When expanding a single large numeric range like {1..10000000}, the sequence generation loop generates all 10 million intermediate elements before the max limit is applied With max=10, the output is correctly limited to 10 items, but the process still allocates ~505 MB and spends ~800ms building the full intermediate array. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.0.6."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45149",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-45149\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: brace-expansion\nFixed Version: 5.0.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-45149](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45149)\nThe brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. From 5.0.0 to before 5.0.6, the max option was being applied too late. When expanding a single large numeric range like {1..10000000}, the sequence generation loop generates all 10 million intermediate elements before the max limit is applied With max=10, the output is correctly limited to 10 items, but the process still allocates ~505 MB and spends ~800ms building the full intermediate array. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.0.6.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-45149**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|brace-expansion|5.0.6|[CVE-2026-45149](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45149)|\n\nThe brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. From 5.0.0 to before 5.0.6, the max option was being applied too late. When expanding a single large numeric range like {1..10000000}, the sequence generation loop generates all 10 million intermediate elements before the max limit is applied With max=10, the output is correctly limited to 10 items, but the process still allocates ~505 MB and spends ~800ms building the full intermediate array. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.0.6."
              },
